From 41d7fdb8bd9fbf1a6b8770abcb9fbaa45ca435e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:53:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tests built and run with the float numerical type

- the libraries of the tests are generated with the numerical type of MGIS
  (real_type option of mfront, MGIS_MFRONT_REAL_TYPE_OPTION).
- the models, only generated in double, are not built in float: the tests
  taking their library accept it as an optional argument.
- RealTypeTest: a behaviour generated with the other numerical type is
  refused at loading, with a message giving both types.
- bit for bit comparisons by a function independent of the type
  (BitwiseEquality.hxx); tolerances written for double adapted to the type
  (Tolerance.hxx): bounded by 10 times the machine epsilon, or given
  explicitly for float when the error depends on the computation (the
  convergence criteria bounded by load, for instance), double unchanged.
- GenericParallelLoadTest compiles the structures of TFEL with the
  numerical type of MGIS before comparing their layouts.
- Norton and NortonFailure: the flow 8e-67 seq^n is written A (seq/K)^n
  with A = 1 and K = (8e-67)^(-1/8.2) Pa, whose coefficients can be
  represented in float (8e-67 can't, and seq^n overflows); Gurson: typed
  literal in a call to min.
Double: 51/51, float: 47/47.
